'' A CALL THROUGH A PROCEDURE POINTER SAYS THE CALLEE'S CONVENTION. The synthetic
'' declaration an indirect call is typed from knew pascal and not stdcall, so on win32
'' every 'function stdcall' pointer call went out cdecl: the callee pops its argument
'' bytes, the caller's esp moves, and every esp-relative local after the call reads
'' garbage. Asserted where it is decided -- the call instruction in the IR.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win32 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/procptr-stdcall.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: call x86_stdcallcc i32 %

'' The direct stdcall call beside it is the control: it was always decorated.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call x86_stdcallcc ptr @"GetProcAddress"